WEBVTT

00:05.304 --> 00:09.035
MAN ON TV: We now return
to Aaron Sorkin 's new show, The Kitchen.

00:09.108 --> 00:10.575
- Where's the milk? No milk?
- We're out. No.

00:10.642 --> 00:12.007
Walk with me.
I want you to get some milk.

00:12.077 --> 00:13.567
- Where? Now?
- At the store. Right now.

00:13.645 --> 00:15.306
- Any store? Bloomie's?
- Any store. Is that a joke?

00:15.381 --> 00:16.473
- What do you think?
- I think we need milk.

00:16.548 --> 00:17.537
I think you're right.

00:17.616 --> 00:18.708
You know, I never
get tired of hearing that.

00:18.784 --> 00:20.479
- Should I go get the milk?
- Go get the milk.

00:21.220 --> 00:22.585
(ALL GROANING)

00:22.654 --> 00:24.178
Looks like the power's out again.

00:24.256 --> 00:27.020
What, are we in Iraq?
This happens entirely too often.

00:27.092 --> 00:29.322
Can we tell stories till it comes back on?

00:29.395 --> 00:33.126
Yeah, Dad. Remember the last time you
told us the story of Star Wars?

00:33.198 --> 00:34.665
Maybe you could tell us another one.

00:34.733 --> 00:35.791
Well, all right.

00:35.868 --> 00:38.564
This is the story of Black Snake Moan.

00:38.637 --> 00:42.334
Once upon a time, Christina Ricci was
all tied up for some reason...

00:42.408 --> 00:44.137
I'm already bored and confused.

00:44.209 --> 00:48.111
Yeah, Dad. Isn't there another story like
Star Wars you could tell us?

00:48.614 --> 00:51.947
There just might be, Chris.
There just might be.

00:59.925 --> 01:02.553
(STAR WARS THEME PLAYING)

02:43.095 --> 02:44.722
CHORUS: (SINGING) His boy Elroy

03:04.883 --> 03:06.908
(MIMICKING PROBE DROID)

03:30.242 --> 03:33.109
Echo 3 to Echo 7.
Han, old buddy, you read me?

03:33.178 --> 03:36.045
Luke, I thought we talked about
this. I changed my code name.

03:36.114 --> 03:39.914
Right. Sorry.
Echo 3 to Carlos Spicy Wiener.

03:39.985 --> 03:41.418
Carlos Spicy Wiener here. Go ahead.

03:41.486 --> 03:43.750
There's a meteorite
that hit the ground near here.

03:43.822 --> 03:45.915
I'm gonna go check it out. Won't take long.

03:45.991 --> 03:48.721
Okay, but be careful.
There's some snow monsters out there.

03:48.794 --> 03:50.557
Relax, Han, I'll be careful...

03:50.629 --> 03:51.653
(SCREAMING)

03:51.730 --> 03:52.924
Cookie!

04:12.684 --> 04:15.676
Hey, you guys, I hate to do this
to you, but I gotta get out of here.

04:15.754 --> 04:18.348
Hey, what's that
on your jacket? Is that the Purina logo?

04:18.423 --> 04:20.118
- No, it's just a patch.
- I like it.

04:20.192 --> 04:21.557
- Thank you.
- I lied. It's lame.

04:21.627 --> 04:23.254
I won't miss you.

04:24.062 --> 04:27.122
Han, wait.
I thought you said you were gonna stay.

04:27.199 --> 04:29.429
Sorry, I can't.
But I'll give you my email address.

04:29.501 --> 04:33.164
It's HanSolo64@CompuServe.com.

04:33.238 --> 04:35.138
- Comp...
- Yes, CompuServe.

04:35.374 --> 04:36.898
But you can't leave now.

04:36.975 --> 04:38.340
You're a natural leader and we...

04:38.410 --> 04:41.243
Hey. Did you guys order some ice?

04:41.813 --> 04:44.008
'Cause I got a bag of ice here.

04:44.082 --> 04:45.913
Thought you might need some ice.

04:46.485 --> 04:49.648
Yes, there is a lot
of ice around here. We get it.

04:49.721 --> 04:52.155
We're having a conversation here.

04:52.224 --> 04:55.022
Hey. I thought
you guys might need some ice.

04:55.093 --> 04:56.924
SOLDIER: What? Why would I need ice?
We're surrounded by...

04:56.995 --> 05:02.160
(LAUGHING) Oh! What a day brightener.

05:02.234 --> 05:03.826
Han, we need you.

05:03.902 --> 05:07.269
- Oh, really? "We" or "I"?
- What do you mean?

05:07.339 --> 05:09.933
You don't want me to leave
because of the way you feel about me.

05:10.008 --> 05:12.704
I bet you're afraid I'm gonna
leave without giving you a goodbye kiss.

05:12.778 --> 05:15.144
Ugh! I'd rather kiss George Takei.

05:15.213 --> 05:17.147
Hello.

05:18.650 --> 05:20.015
(CHUCKLING)

05:21.787 --> 05:23.254
Man, it's cold in here.

05:23.322 --> 05:27.725
Beep-boop-beep. I like all these
electrical wires just nailed to the ice.

05:27.793 --> 05:29.488
That's probably pretty safe, right?

05:30.028 --> 05:31.757
Captain Solo, have you seen Master Luke?

05:31.830 --> 05:33.127
'Cause no one knows where he is.

05:33.198 --> 05:35.189
What? Well, that doesn't sound good.

05:35.267 --> 05:37.861
All right, I'm gonna go out
and look for him. I'll take my Don Don.

05:37.936 --> 05:41.394
Well, I can't go outside. It's cold out there.

05:41.473 --> 05:44.101
You can't go out there
in this weather. Your Don Don will freeze.

05:44.176 --> 05:45.541
Then I'll see you in hell!

05:45.610 --> 05:47.009
SOLDIER: Wait, Han. You'll need this.

05:47.079 --> 05:49.707
- What?
- (SNICKERING) Bag of ice.

05:49.781 --> 05:52.682
You knucklehead.
Get out of here, but know I love you.

06:01.293 --> 06:02.453
(GRUNTS)

06:03.762 --> 06:05.923
Damn these stubby arms!

06:17.909 --> 06:20.241
Well, this is no better.

06:23.148 --> 06:24.206
(SCREAMING)

06:24.282 --> 06:25.476
(GASPS)

06:28.854 --> 06:32.950
Me was going to ask you
to snow monster ball, but now forget it!

06:33.024 --> 06:34.286
(SOBBING)

07:01.586 --> 07:06.216
OBI-WAN: Luke. Luke,
pull your pants down.

07:07.392 --> 07:08.450
Ben?

07:08.527 --> 07:10.188
You look awful cold.

07:10.262 --> 07:13.857
Why don't I get you
a nice hot bowl of Zima soup?

07:13.932 --> 07:15.024
Ben.

07:15.100 --> 07:16.124
Luke.

07:16.201 --> 07:21.696
You will go to the Dagobah system and
learn the ways of the Force from Yoda.

07:21.773 --> 07:23.070
Ben.

07:28.447 --> 07:30.005
- Luke!
- Ben!

07:30.081 --> 07:31.173
Hang on, kid.

07:31.249 --> 07:34.309
Yoda. Dagobah system.

07:34.753 --> 07:38.883
Zima soup. Yoda. Dagobah.

07:39.458 --> 07:42.689
Last time I was in a Dago bar
I was drinking a beer in Little Italy.

07:42.761 --> 07:44.023
Go on, get out of here!

07:44.095 --> 07:47.929
Well, I can't stand
this cold anymore. I'm gonna die.

07:48.433 --> 07:49.457
Oh!

07:49.534 --> 07:51.024
Well, it's probably for the best.

07:51.102 --> 07:55.038
There are way too many
elderly comedians out here in the snow.

08:01.213 --> 08:04.376
This may smell bad, kid,
but it'll keep you warm.

08:04.716 --> 08:05.944
(SIGHS)

08:06.284 --> 08:08.445
I thought they smelled bad

08:08.653 --> 08:09.915
(GASPING)

08:21.333 --> 08:23.062
on the outside.

08:32.677 --> 08:36.408
Captain Solo, do you copy?
This is Overweight Pilot Number One.

08:36.481 --> 08:38.847
Commander Skywalker, do you copy?

08:38.917 --> 08:40.145
HAN: Who are you looking for?

08:40.218 --> 08:41.685
Captain Solo, there you are!

08:41.753 --> 08:44.415
I'm sorry, I didn't copy that.
Who are you looking for?

08:45.257 --> 08:47.589
Carlos Spicy Wiener, do you copy?

08:47.659 --> 08:49.251
Carlos Spicy Wiener here, go ahead.

08:55.233 --> 08:57.531
They found us, kid.
We're going back to base.

08:57.602 --> 09:00.969
Just as soon as I grab some powder
with these skiing young people.

09:01.072 --> 09:02.767
(JUICY FRUIT THEME PLAYING)

09:06.645 --> 09:09.739
MAN: (SINGING) Get your skis shined up
Grab a stick of Juicy Fruit

09:09.814 --> 09:12.374
The taste is gonna move ya

09:12.450 --> 09:15.010
Take a sniff
Pull it out

09:15.854 --> 09:20.086
The taste is gonna move ya
when you pop it in your mouth

09:20.158 --> 09:22.922
Juicy Fruit is gonna move ya

09:22.994 --> 09:26.020
It chews so soft, it gets right to ya

09:26.097 --> 09:27.155
Juicy Fruit

09:27.232 --> 09:30.793
The taste, the taste, the taste
is gonna move ya

09:33.271 --> 09:34.295
How you doing, kid?

09:34.372 --> 09:36.966
You look strong enough
to pull the ears off Jennifer Garner.

09:37.042 --> 09:38.270
Thanks to you.

09:38.343 --> 09:41.005
Well, your managed-to-keep-me-around-
a-little-longerness,

09:41.079 --> 09:43.547
it looks like you managed
to keep me around a little longer.

09:43.615 --> 09:46.049
I assure you, I had nothing to do with it.

09:46.117 --> 09:47.209
Yeah, right.

09:47.285 --> 09:50.379
I think you just can't stand
to let a fat guy like me out of your sight.

09:50.455 --> 09:55.654
Why, you stuck up,
half-witted, scruffy-looking nerf herder!

09:56.494 --> 09:59.986
You can't use that word!
Only we can use that word!

10:24.522 --> 10:26.456
(GASPS) The boss is coming. Look busy.

10:26.524 --> 10:28.048
- Lot of Empire stuff to do.
- Empire stuff.

10:28.126 --> 10:30.026
- Getting Empire stuff done.
- Busy with Empire stuff.

10:30.095 --> 10:32.029
- Yes, this is good Empire stuff.
- This Empire stuff looks good.

10:32.097 --> 10:33.758
Yes, I think we're done
with this Empire stuff.

10:34.265 --> 10:35.857
Hey, dudes, what you looking at?

10:35.934 --> 10:37.561
We think we found something.

10:37.669 --> 10:39.534
(PROBE DROID CHATTERING)

10:40.238 --> 10:42.468
That's it. The Rebels are there.

10:42.540 --> 10:45.270
My lord, there are so many
uncharted settlements.

10:45.343 --> 10:48.642
It could be a phony! A big, fat phony!

10:48.847 --> 10:50.371
What'd them Rebels do anyways?

10:50.448 --> 10:52.746
- You know your friend Alan?
- Yeah, I like Alan.

10:52.817 --> 10:56.776
- They took his dog.
- (GASPS) They took Zeus? Oh, no!

10:56.855 --> 10:59.221
- Central Command to Jeffrey.
- Jeffrey here.

10:59.290 --> 11:02.020
- Jeffrey, them Rebels took Zeus.
- That's Alan 's dog.

11:02.093 --> 11:04.527
- I know.
- Oh, no!

11:04.596 --> 11:05.790
I know.

11:06.097 --> 11:08.565
Set your course for the Hoth system.

11:12.470 --> 11:14.438
Hey, take care of yourself, Chewie.

11:14.539 --> 11:17.406
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!
What's this handshake business, huh?

11:17.475 --> 11:20.911
Come here. Come on.
Come on, bring it in. Come on. Come on.

11:20.979 --> 11:22.571
I'm not really a hug person.

11:22.647 --> 11:25.343
Knock it off. Come here. Come on, bring it.

11:25.417 --> 11:27.749
Yeah, yeah. Hug it out, bitch.

11:27.819 --> 11:29.787
Hug it out, yeah.
Spray that hug all over me.

11:29.854 --> 11:31.048
What's wrong with you?

11:31.122 --> 11:34.023
What? I just wanna share
my throbbing emotions

11:34.092 --> 11:35.457
and shoot hot hug all over you.

11:35.527 --> 11:37.085
I don't get why that's a problem.

11:37.162 --> 11:39.630
Hey, Luke. Take care of yourself, okay?

11:39.698 --> 11:40.756
You, too.

11:40.832 --> 11:42.959
Hey, what'd you end up doing
with that dog we kidnapped?

11:43.034 --> 11:44.661
I killed it and ate it!

11:44.736 --> 11:45.964
- Yeah! Yeah!
- Yeah!

11:46.037 --> 11:47.902
- Rebels! Rebels!
- Rebels!

11:47.972 --> 11:49.371
- Empire sucks!
- Rebels!

11:49.441 --> 11:52.410
- Rebels! Yeah!
- Yeah, Rebels! Yeah.

12:05.990 --> 12:07.617
Lord Vader,
we've entered the Hoth system,

12:07.692 --> 12:10.661
but the Rebels have put up
an energy shield blocking our entry.

12:10.729 --> 12:12.026
What are we gonna do now, buddy?

12:12.097 --> 12:14.497
Admiral Ozzel came out
of light speed too quickly.

12:14.566 --> 12:18.229
(CHUCKLING) Yeah. I had that problem
with a chick the other night.

12:18.303 --> 12:21.864
Okay, gross. I'm gonna
turn around and take care of this other guy.

12:22.674 --> 12:25.370
Lord Vader, we're out of light speed and...

12:25.443 --> 12:26.535
(CHOKING)

12:26.611 --> 12:29.307
You have failed me
for the last time, Admiral.

12:29.547 --> 12:31.981
Didn't know I could choke you
through the TV, did you?

12:32.050 --> 12:35.542
Well, I can.
Captain Piett, you're in charge now.

12:35.620 --> 12:38.555
Don't fail me, Admiral Piett.

12:38.857 --> 12:40.984
A promotion? Really?

12:41.059 --> 12:43.425
Can I get business cards
that say "Admiral"?

12:43.495 --> 12:46.191
That's not in the budget. You know,
we're trying to catch Rebels here.

12:46.264 --> 12:48.562
I don't even have business cards.
None of us do.

12:48.633 --> 12:50.157
- Do you have business cards?
- Yeah.

12:50.235 --> 12:52.465
You have business cards?
You're a stormtrooper.

12:52.537 --> 12:55.131
There's like a million of you.
What do you need business cards for?

12:55.206 --> 12:56.503
Well, they're for my cookie business.

12:56.574 --> 12:58.769
I don't want... Oh, my God.

12:58.843 --> 13:02.472
(CHUCKLING) That chocolate chip cookie
looks like the Death Star.

13:05.750 --> 13:07.615
May I have everyone's attention please?

13:07.685 --> 13:09.676
We're evacuating into outer space,

13:09.754 --> 13:12.484
with literally
infinite directions in which to flee.

13:12.557 --> 13:14.923
However, we have decided
that our transports

13:14.993 --> 13:17.860
will travel directly toward
the fleet of Star Destroyers.

13:17.929 --> 13:20.090
- Any questions?
- Yeah.

13:20.165 --> 13:24.067
Is there someone from the military
we can talk to? A man, perhaps?

13:30.742 --> 13:32.869
Sir, Rebel ships are coming into our sector.

13:32.944 --> 13:35.139
Good. Our first catch of the day.

13:35.213 --> 13:36.840
(SCOFFS) Like you know how to fish.

13:37.282 --> 13:39.546
Prepare to fire giant boob-nipple gun.

13:42.654 --> 13:44.019
(CHUCKLING)

14:00.672 --> 14:01.696
Feeling okay, sir?

14:01.773 --> 14:04.003
Just like new. How about you, Dack?

14:04.075 --> 14:06.976
I feel like I could take on
the whole Empire myself.

14:07.045 --> 14:09.741
Really? 'Cause that would be awesome.

14:09.814 --> 14:12.544
Hey, everyone, Dack says he's got this one.

14:12.617 --> 14:14.107
(ALL CHEERING)

14:14.319 --> 14:16.150
You know it, bitches!

14:23.194 --> 14:26.823
Hey, Imperial fleet,
get ready to suck some Dack!

14:35.573 --> 14:37.006
- I think we're doomed.
- Nah.

14:37.075 --> 14:40.533
Unless they've got any big, giant
robot camels, I think we're okay.

14:43.982 --> 14:46.007
Jim, robot camels.

14:51.122 --> 14:53.886
Check it out, that one's wearing Crocs.

14:59.063 --> 15:00.587
(MEN SCREAMING)

15:01.566 --> 15:04.000
Echo Station 5-7, we are on our way.

15:04.068 --> 15:05.228
REBEL LEADER: Great. We'll see you in...

15:05.303 --> 15:07.328
(GUN FIRING)

15:07.805 --> 15:09.932
Echo Station 5-8, we are on our way.

15:10.074 --> 15:11.166
Hurry!

15:26.791 --> 15:29.191
Yes, Lord Vader,
their shield will be down in moments.

15:29.260 --> 15:30.488
You may start your landing.

15:30.561 --> 15:32.756
Excellent. We'll prepare for our descent.

15:32.830 --> 15:34.821
Hey. Hey, Consuela, no cleaning.

15:34.899 --> 15:38.198
No cleaning while I'm doing
the hologram... Shut that off!

15:38.269 --> 15:43.366
Mr. Darth, you no have
no more Windex on Star Destroyer.

15:43.441 --> 15:45.807
Well, that's not my problem.
Why don’t you go out and buy some?

15:45.877 --> 15:48.209
No. No, you buy.

15:48.279 --> 15:50.747
What if I give you the money,
then you can go out and buy it?

15:50.815 --> 15:52.043
No.

16:10.835 --> 16:12.097
(EXCLAIMING)

16:12.303 --> 16:13.634
(GROANING)

16:44.569 --> 16:46.469
Crap! I'm hit!

16:53.611 --> 16:54.805
(GASPS)

16:56.614 --> 16:58.741
FEMALE VOICE: On Star.
What is the nature of your emergency?

16:58.816 --> 17:02.081
Yeah, I just got laser torpedoed
by an Imperial walker

17:02.153 --> 17:03.780
and I need roadside assistance.

17:03.888 --> 17:07.051
Of course, sir.
Am I speaking with Admiral Ackbar?

17:07.125 --> 17:10.356
Yeah. Yes. Yes, I'm Admiral Ackbar.

17:10.428 --> 17:11.554
(HOARSELY) It's a trap.

17:15.533 --> 17:18.969
(SLURRING) I love you guys.
We had a great summer.

17:22.140 --> 17:23.971
Han! What are you still doing here?

17:24.042 --> 17:28.138
Well, I just realized that my spaceship
works better when I have the keys.

17:28.212 --> 17:29.270
Duh!

17:31.115 --> 17:33.583
MAN ON PA: Imperial troops have entered
the base. Imperial troops have...

17:33.651 --> 17:34.982
(FEEDBACK)

17:35.119 --> 17:38.452
Sorry, I dropped the thing.
Imperial troops have entered the base.

17:57.241 --> 17:59.334
(GASPS) Oh, my God, it's pregnant.

17:59.710 --> 18:01.610
We're in a war. We're in a war.

18:18.129 --> 18:20.791
I want the princess captured immediately.

18:20.865 --> 18:24.665
Geez, Gordon, maybe today wasn't the day
to wear your mesh stormtrooper shirt.

18:24.735 --> 18:28.330
Sorry, it's just...
I'm going out dancing after work tonight.

18:28.406 --> 18:32.206
Oh, my God, I can't remember
the last time I went out dancing.

18:32.276 --> 18:35.143
I think it was Memorial Day,
like, two years ago.

18:35.213 --> 18:36.805
No, you know what? It was four years ago.

18:36.881 --> 18:38.348
You know how long it was?

18:38.416 --> 18:41.510
It was on Alderaan.
That's how long ago it was.

18:42.453 --> 18:45.422
Are those guys getting away?
We should probably get those guys.

18:45.490 --> 18:48.687
Those other guys will get them.
So, what else?

18:53.297 --> 18:55.857
This bucket of bolts
is never gonna get us past that blockade.

18:55.933 --> 18:57.958
This bucket's got a few surprises
left in her.

18:58.035 --> 19:00.367
Plus, me and Chewie are on it.
Ain't that right, Chewie?

19:00.438 --> 19:03.737
- Hell, yeah. You my nerf herder.
- You my nerf herder.

19:03.808 --> 19:05.332
All right, Chewie, punch it.

19:13.284 --> 19:15.115
Thank God that hot chick is gone.

19:15.186 --> 19:17.177
Now I can let loose my Darth farts.

19:17.255 --> 19:18.279
(FARTS)

19:18.356 --> 19:19.345
(AIR HISSING)

19:19.423 --> 19:20.412
(FARTS)

19:20.525 --> 19:21.822
(AIR HISSING)

19:23.494 --> 19:25.359
Artoo, get her ready for takeoff.

19:25.429 --> 19:28.159
You may not remember,
but I told you last week

19:28.232 --> 19:30.666
I got my niece's recital today.

19:31.302 --> 19:33.293
(VIOLIN PLAYING OFF-KEY)

19:37.675 --> 19:41.634
- We gotta sit through this whole thing?
- It's not that much longer.

19:41.712 --> 19:44.943
She's number seven
and there's, like, 18 people.

19:45.016 --> 19:46.381
Relax, man.

19:46.517 --> 19:48.382
I mean,
as long as she knows you were here...

19:48.452 --> 19:51.216
Look, this is happening,
so just come to peace with it.

19:58.829 --> 20:00.922
Hey, this ain't the way
to the rendezvous point.

20:01.199 --> 20:02.689
We're not meeting up with the others.

20:02.767 --> 20:04.200
We're going to the Dagobah system.

20:08.406 --> 20:09.873
Hi. Excuse me. Excuse me.

20:09.941 --> 20:12.205
Hi, yeah, do you know
how to get to the Dagobah system?

20:12.276 --> 20:15.040
Yeah, actually
we're headed there now. You can follow us.

20:15.112 --> 20:18.809
Okay, great.
Annoying question. We have to get gas,

20:18.883 --> 20:21.443
would you mind pulling off
and waiting for us while we do that?

20:21.519 --> 20:22.577
(GROANS)

20:22.653 --> 20:24.314
Thank you so much.

20:24.989 --> 20:26.013
(SIGHING)

20:40.204 --> 20:41.671
Han, look!

20:41.739 --> 20:43.570
HAN: Crap, there's two more of them
dead ahead.

20:44.475 --> 20:46.568
It's all right,
I think I can outmaneuver them.

20:55.720 --> 20:59.121
JOHN BUNNELL: This Rebel lawbreaker
thinks he can outrun the Empire.

20:59.190 --> 21:02.751
The pursuing officers
realize he's entered a residential area.

21:02.827 --> 21:06.490
They give him a wide berth,
but they don 't let him out of their sight.

21:06.564 --> 21:11.092
Astonishingly, the driver makes a left,
right into an asteroid field.

21:11.168 --> 21:14.831
What are you doing? You're not actually
going into an asteroid field.

21:14.905 --> 21:17.169
Well, it's either that
or go into the strawberry fields.

21:17.742 --> 21:20.302
Hey, you know what
I'm getting into? Is one-legged chicks.

21:20.378 --> 21:22.778
Yeah, Paul,
what's your new wife's name? Peg?

21:22.847 --> 21:24.212
That'll be enough of that, lad.

21:24.282 --> 21:25.306
How about Eileen?

21:25.383 --> 21:26.714
Ringo got it.

21:32.023 --> 21:35.891
Sir, the odds of successfully
navigating an asteroid field are two to one.

21:35.960 --> 21:39.487
Never tell me the...
Actually, that's not bad.

21:39.730 --> 21:41.391
Yeah. No, let's keep going.

22:02.453 --> 22:06.514
Look at that one! Look at that one there!
Look at that other one!

22:06.590 --> 22:07.921
(SCREAMING)

22:07.992 --> 22:09.789
We're gonna get pulverized out here!

22:09.860 --> 22:12.090
Look, we got four or five
of the main characters on this ship.

22:12.163 --> 22:13.323
I think we'll be fine.

22:33.517 --> 22:35.451
There, that looks good.

22:36.320 --> 22:39.756
Doesn't that pie look good?
Too bad we can't get at it.

22:39.824 --> 22:41.689
It's in space, and we're in here.

22:41.759 --> 22:44.125
Otherwise, I'd be eating it right now.

22:44.195 --> 22:45.719
All right, let's park right there in that cave.

22:47.898 --> 22:50.162
What are you doing? You can't park there.

22:51.202 --> 22:53.466
- You're not handicapped.
- I have vertigo.

22:53.537 --> 22:55.334
It's a real medical condition.

22:55.406 --> 22:58.466
I'm just going on record
as saying I'm not comfortable with this.

23:07.952 --> 23:09.920
I hope you know what you're doing.

23:10.287 --> 23:13.450
I've just found
that Leia's constant questioning of me

23:13.524 --> 23:16.652
has not been productive
to the atmosphere of the ship.

23:16.727 --> 23:20.254
And I think that she just
needs to get some respect for herself.

23:25.736 --> 23:29.729
Artoo, wake up, we're here.
Put your shoes on.

23:29.807 --> 23:31.502
You better hurry up and land.

23:31.575 --> 23:34.874
The last half hour,
I've been having all pee dreams.

23:38.482 --> 23:40.950
All the scopes are dead! I can't see a thing!

23:41.452 --> 23:45.286
Sorry, that's me.
I was still using an electronic device.

23:45.790 --> 23:49.282
Okay, that's much better.
Now I can see the swamp... The swamp!

23:58.068 --> 24:01.003
Swamp crashes.
They can land you knee-deep in trouble.

24:01.071 --> 24:05.064
But the "good hands" people at Allstate will
make sure you have a soft landing.

24:05.142 --> 24:08.475
Professional service.
Non-threatening black spokesperson.

24:08.546 --> 24:10.013
That's Allstate's stand.

24:12.450 --> 24:16.181
Thank God for these airbags.
You okay back there?

24:16.253 --> 24:20.019
I'm okay, but the midget
inside me's got a head concussion.

24:25.362 --> 24:27.296
No, no, no, no, no, no!

24:29.266 --> 24:30.665
Artoo?

24:41.245 --> 24:42.769
Artoo!

24:43.948 --> 24:45.609
(ARTOO SCREAMING)

24:48.085 --> 24:50.451
Artoo, are you okay?

24:50.521 --> 24:54.252
I think so. Boy, who knows
what else is in this swamp?

24:55.926 --> 24:57.791
SUPER FRIENDS ANNOUNCER:
Meanwhile, at the Legion of Doom!

24:57.862 --> 24:59.329
- Not now!
- Okay.

24:59.997 --> 25:01.521
(EERIE SILENCE)

25:01.599 --> 25:02.827
(CAWING)

25:06.036 --> 25:07.367
YODA: Hey, who the hell are you?

25:08.372 --> 25:10.602
What the hell is that creepy little thing?

25:10.674 --> 25:12.335
Well, I'm not Yoda.

25:12.610 --> 25:13.770
Okay, I'm Yoda.

25:13.844 --> 25:15.209
You're Yoda?

25:15.479 --> 25:18.175
You're the one
that Obi-Wan sent me here to find.

25:18.249 --> 25:20.274
Will you teach me the ways of the Force?

25:20.351 --> 25:23.445
No, I will not teach you
the ways of the Force.

25:23.521 --> 25:25.853
Okay, I'll teach you the ways of the Force.

25:25.923 --> 25:29.381
But if you want to become a Jedi,
first I gotta ask you something.

25:29.460 --> 25:30.688
Did you see Van Wilder?

25:30.761 --> 25:32.194
Yeah, I saw it on Comedy Central.

25:32.263 --> 25:36.859
No! No, no, no, no, no!
We got a lot of training to do.

25:36.934 --> 25:39.232
I'm asking, did you see
the DVD frat house edition

25:39.303 --> 25:42.136
with all the uncensored footage
and the interview with Ryan Reynolds?

25:42.206 --> 25:43.264
No.

25:43.340 --> 25:45.968
Well, that's all part
of mastering the Force, man.

25:46.043 --> 25:48.978
It starts with
checking out sweet-ass DVD releases,

25:49.046 --> 25:51.879
like Iron Man, directed by Jon Favreau.

25:51.949 --> 25:54.747
Yeah, he puts himself
in his own movies, but you don't mind

25:54.818 --> 25:57.981
'cause he seems like the kind of guy
who'd help you move if you asked him.

26:06.530 --> 26:08.896
I'm glad you're here.
Look, I pulled this all apart,

26:08.966 --> 26:10.900
and it looks like
you're gonna need a new condenser.

26:10.968 --> 26:12.230
Really? A new condenser?

26:12.303 --> 26:13.634
Yeah, and I would also highly recommend

26:13.704 --> 26:16.172
a complete flush
of your photon conversion system.

26:16.240 --> 26:17.639
I swear I just did that.

26:17.708 --> 26:19.767
Okay, well, how about this?
Do you want me to just go ahead

26:19.843 --> 26:22.368
and do that
while I'm replacing the new condenser?

26:22.446 --> 26:25.313
I think I'd like to call my husband.

26:25.382 --> 26:26.508
Look, how about this?

26:26.584 --> 26:28.677
You buy the condenser,
and I'll make out with you.

26:28.752 --> 26:29.912
(EXCLAIMS)

26:29.987 --> 26:31.614
I'm gonna kiss you so hard,

26:31.689 --> 26:34.783
the picture's gonna change
into something else.

26:41.932 --> 26:44.992
Look, this isn't Windex
but it's just as good. It's the store brand.

26:45.069 --> 26:49.301
- No. No. It leave a film.
- I'm okay with the film. Just use it.

26:49.373 --> 26:53.639
- No. No. I no can clean.
- Shit.

26:53.711 --> 26:54.973
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

26:55.045 --> 26:56.706
- Hello?
- Mr. Darth Vader...

26:56.780 --> 27:00.079
Yes, sir. Quiet, quiet. It's the Emperor.

27:00.150 --> 27:02.846
- It's the Emperor.
- Tell him I no can do Friday.

27:02.920 --> 27:05.047
- Okay. Okay, okay. Sir... Yeah.
- My apartment need water.

27:05.122 --> 27:06.350
- No, no. No.
- He need to get it fixed.

27:06.423 --> 27:09.517
(STUTTERING) Hello? I can't hear you.

27:09.593 --> 27:12.756
I'm going to the knee pad.
I'm gonna call you from the knee pad.

27:22.640 --> 27:24.870
What is thy bidding, my master?

27:24.942 --> 27:27.240
Hey, I'm downloading
all my music to my iPod

27:27.311 --> 27:28.778
'cause I'm getting rid of my CDs.

27:28.846 --> 27:31.110
Do you have any desire for
Natalie Merchant's Tigerlily?

27:31.181 --> 27:32.239
No.

27:32.316 --> 27:34.910
- Alanis Morissette's Jagged Little Pill?
- No.

27:34.985 --> 27:37.010
You sure? This thing was unstoppable.

27:37.087 --> 27:39.612
This was the soundtrack to my '95.

27:39.690 --> 27:42.853
- To my '95 and my '96, actually.
- No, thank you.

27:42.926 --> 27:45.053
- Richard Marx, Hold On To The Night?
- (EXCITEDLY) Yes!

27:45.129 --> 27:46.858
(STUTTERING) I mean... Yeah, no...

27:46.930 --> 27:48.898
I mean, if you're giving stuff away,
yeah, sure.

27:48.966 --> 27:49.990
All right, listen.

27:50.067 --> 27:53.230
It turns out
Anakin Skywalker's son is still alive.

27:53.303 --> 27:55.669
I'm gonna need you
to find him and turn him.

27:55.739 --> 27:58.674
Really? Maybe I can make him go bi,
but all the way is gonna be tough.

27:58.742 --> 28:00.505
No, I mean, turn him to the dark side.

28:00.577 --> 28:01.601
Well, yeah, I thought that's what you...

28:01.679 --> 28:03.078
- Oh, of the Force.
- Yes.

28:03.147 --> 28:05.274
I'll get him over to the dark side.

28:05.416 --> 28:07.281
I'll just show him our recruiting video.

28:07.518 --> 28:09.486
(CHEERFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

28:14.158 --> 28:16.422
Thanks to the training
I received in the Empire,

28:16.493 --> 28:19.189
I have all the skills I need
to make it in the real world.

28:20.631 --> 28:24.260
The Empire GI Bill
helped me finish school. Hey, wait up!

28:25.102 --> 28:28.469
And I met my wife in the service.
We had our honeymoon on Alderaan.

28:28.639 --> 28:30.266
WOMAN: Good thing
we took pictures, huh?

28:30.340 --> 28:31.671
(LAUGHING)

28:32.009 --> 28:34.500
RECRUITMENT ANNOUNCER:
The Empire, chasing Rebel scum,

28:35.079 --> 28:36.637
killing Luke's aunt and uncle,

28:37.114 --> 28:38.945
telling people to move along.

28:39.416 --> 28:42.647
The Empire, our ships are big triangles.

28:47.357 --> 28:50.190
That's good. Stretch it out, stretch it out

28:50.260 --> 28:51.750
because we're gonna start the training.

28:51.829 --> 28:55.663
I'm ready, Master Yoda.
I'm ready to become a Jedi.

28:55.733 --> 28:58.065
All right, kid, let's do it.

28:58.168 --> 29:00.398
(ROCKY IV THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

29:14.118 --> 29:15.483
(INAUDIBLE)

30:10.607 --> 30:11.665
You know, I'm up for this,

30:11.742 --> 30:15.610
but it kind of feels
like the dark side has a better gym than us.

30:29.092 --> 30:31.117
(DISTANT EXPLOSIONS)

30:43.507 --> 30:44.769
(SCREAMS)

30:45.776 --> 30:47.437
There's something out there.

30:50.514 --> 30:51.538
Hmm?

30:51.615 --> 30:53.549
- There's something out there.
- Where?

30:53.617 --> 30:55.141
Out there, in the cave!

30:55.219 --> 30:57.710
(LAUGHS) Crazy women,
always hearing things.

30:57.788 --> 31:00.154
- There's something out there.
- Let's go check it out.

31:03.961 --> 31:06.088
What's all this slime on the floor?

31:06.163 --> 31:08.597
Yeah. It feels like we're
in Rod Stewart's stomach.

31:12.536 --> 31:14.026
Wait a minute.

31:15.239 --> 31:16.536
Hang on a second.

31:18.008 --> 31:19.498
What's going on here?

31:21.111 --> 31:22.544
Something doesn't add up.

31:24.147 --> 31:25.409
Just a minute.

31:26.717 --> 31:27.775
Time out.

31:29.386 --> 31:30.944
This ain't quite right.

31:32.389 --> 31:33.913
Now I get it. We should go.

31:37.728 --> 31:40.094
Hang on, sweetheart. We're taking off.

31:45.669 --> 31:47.136
LEIA: The cave is collapsing!

31:47.204 --> 31:48.831
- This is no cave.
- What?

32:01.518 --> 32:03.918
How come I never get
any lines in these things?

32:03.987 --> 32:05.750
PETER: Shut up, Meg.

32:15.232 --> 32:17.996
All right. Let's take a break.
Your back's getting all sweaty.

32:18.068 --> 32:19.695
Sorry. Does that.

32:20.037 --> 32:22.028
All right.
Now, let's go over what we've learned.

32:22.105 --> 32:25.097
- Naked chicks. Best?
- Rebecca De Mornay in Risky Business.

32:25.175 --> 32:27.336
- Good. Worst?
- Kathy Bates in About Schmidt.

32:27.411 --> 32:31.142
Correct. I also would've accepted
the rotting old woman in The Shining,

32:31.214 --> 32:34.149
but Kathy Bates is probably worse.
Best scene in Teen Wolf?

32:34.217 --> 32:35.707
When Michael J. Fox is in the bathroom,

32:35.786 --> 32:37.310
turning into a werewolf for the first time

32:37.387 --> 32:39.548
and his dad's
knocking on the door and he is freaking out

32:39.623 --> 32:42.217
and he opens the door
and his dad's a werewolf, too.

32:42.292 --> 32:43.281
Gold star.

32:43.360 --> 32:45.851
I would've also accepted the scene
at the end, at the basketball game,

32:45.929 --> 32:48.056
where the guy
in the crowd has his dick out.

32:48.131 --> 32:49.758
- What?
- Yeah, there's a guy at the end.

32:49.833 --> 32:52.563
Go online. Look it up.
He's in the stands, way in the background,

32:52.636 --> 32:55.070
and he's totally got his dick out.

32:55.739 --> 32:58.799
What's in there? It feels cold.

32:59.009 --> 33:01.944
That place is strong with the dark side.

33:02.312 --> 33:05.645
But it's very confusing
and it stops the movie dead.

33:05.716 --> 33:07.809
I'm going in there anyway.

33:15.425 --> 33:16.619
(GASPS)

33:33.443 --> 33:36.810
You know, I guess we should take
advantage of this very rare opportunity.

33:36.880 --> 33:39.212
(CHEERFUL MUSIC PLAYING ON PIANO)

33:39.516 --> 33:42.610
BOTH: (SINGING) You and I will settle down

33:42.686 --> 33:47.919
In a cottage built for two

33:47.991 --> 33:49.618
Dear little buttercup

33:49.693 --> 33:51.718
Sweet little buttercup

33:51.795 --> 33:53.763
My little buttercup

33:53.864 --> 33:58.358
I love you

34:05.042 --> 34:07.067
- I hate these hats.
- Yes, sir.

34:07.544 --> 34:09.774
DARTH VADER: Okay,
nice bounty hunter turnout today.

34:10.247 --> 34:14.581
Let's see, we got Robot Guy,
Old Timey Deep Sea Diver Looking Guy,

34:14.651 --> 34:18.246
Lizard Guy, who I think
I saw get in a fight with Captain Kirk,

34:18.321 --> 34:20.755
Boba Fett, of course,
thanks for coming, and...

34:21.058 --> 34:22.252
What are you supposed to be?

34:22.325 --> 34:24.020
Raggedy Andy.

34:24.194 --> 34:27.129
Get the fuck out
of my bounty hunter meeting.

34:32.536 --> 34:36.336
Okay, get ready to go to light speed.
One, two, three.

34:36.406 --> 34:39.807
(ENGINE STALLING)

34:39.876 --> 34:42.777
(SINGING MOCKINGLY)
Whanh! Whanh! Whanh! Whanh!

34:42.846 --> 34:43.835
Crap.

34:43.914 --> 34:44.972
No light speed?

34:45.048 --> 34:46.379
No light speed.

34:50.987 --> 34:53.182
I got an idea. Chewie, turn us around.

34:53.256 --> 34:54.553
You're gonna attack them?

34:54.624 --> 34:56.421
(MIMICKING) "You're gonna attack them?"

34:56.493 --> 34:57.585
That's how you sound.

34:57.661 --> 34:59.356
(SQUEAKILY) "You're gonna attack them?"

34:59.429 --> 35:00.726
Imagine listening to that all day.

35:06.369 --> 35:07.802
They're moving into attack position.

35:07.871 --> 35:08.997
Good. Put the shields up.

35:09.072 --> 35:11.336
Oh, my God! You have cake?
Where'd you get cake?

35:11.408 --> 35:13.638
It was Jim's birthday,
but I think it's all gone.

35:21.418 --> 35:23.613
Track them.
They may come around for another attack.

35:23.687 --> 35:26.281
Captain, the ship
no longer appears on our scopes.

35:26.356 --> 35:29.519
They can't have disappeared.
No ship that small has a cloaking device.

35:29.593 --> 35:33.051
Captain, Lord Vader demands an update
on the pursuit of the Millennium Falcon.

35:33.263 --> 35:36.255
(STUTTERING) Tell him...
Tell him we blew it up.

35:37.300 --> 35:39.291
He's not on hold and he just heard you.

35:39.369 --> 35:40.563
DARTH VADER: Yeah, I just heard you.

35:40.637 --> 35:41.831
(CHOKING)

35:51.781 --> 35:54.147
This is insane, Han!
They're gonna find us here.

35:54.217 --> 35:56.981
Yeah, and even if they don't,
where are we gonna hide out after this?

35:57.053 --> 35:58.543
Hey, what about Lando?

35:58.622 --> 36:00.214
The Lando system?

36:00.290 --> 36:02.588
Lando's not a system. He's a black guy.

36:02.692 --> 36:05.092
In fact, I think he might be
the only black guy in the galaxy.

36:05.162 --> 36:06.754
(CHUCKLES) Let's hope, right?

36:06.863 --> 36:08.330
ALL: Whoa!

36:08.398 --> 36:09.763
(CLANKING)

36:09.833 --> 36:11.266
All right, the fleet's breaking up.

36:11.334 --> 36:13.029
Chewie, get ready
to release the landing claw

36:13.103 --> 36:15.663
and we'll float away
with their garbage. Release!

36:21.778 --> 36:23.803
Look at that. Space bums.

36:28.952 --> 36:31.443
Let's be thankful
for what we have, everyone.

36:31.521 --> 36:33.079
Be thankful for what we have.

36:33.156 --> 36:34.180
(THUD)

36:34.257 --> 36:36.919
Oh, my God, I hit a space bum!
Chewie, go, go, go, go!

36:45.235 --> 36:47.169
All right, concentrate.

36:48.371 --> 36:49.360
What do you see?

36:49.439 --> 36:52.533
I see a woman draining your bank account

36:52.609 --> 36:55.373
and running off with a real estate agent.

36:55.445 --> 36:57.436
That is a bitch you see.

36:57.514 --> 37:01.644
And I see my friends.
They're in trouble! I gotta save them!

37:03.153 --> 37:06.611
Wait, wait, wait. Luke, that's a stupid idea.
You're not done with all your Force stuff.

37:06.690 --> 37:08.590
And besides, you can't fight Vader.

37:08.658 --> 37:11.183
Only an experienced Jedi
could fight Vader.

37:11.261 --> 37:13.161
Well, why don't you go?

37:13.797 --> 37:16.027
Yeah, you're probably ready to fight Vader.

37:22.205 --> 37:25.197
That boy was our last hope.

37:25.475 --> 37:28.000
No, there is another.

37:28.511 --> 37:31.275
I know. I have the Force, too, you know.

37:40.857 --> 37:45.521
I don't have a landing permit.
I'm trying to reach Lando Calrissian.

37:46.062 --> 37:47.552
What the hell's he firing at me for?

37:47.831 --> 37:50.026
- I told you not to shoot.
- Well, you're not in charge. I am.

37:50.100 --> 37:51.192
- Well, I'm steering.
- No, I'm steering.

37:51.268 --> 37:52.360
- No, I am.
- I have a steering wheel.

37:52.435 --> 37:53.766
- So do I. There's two.
- Well, that's stupid.

37:53.837 --> 37:55.134
- I know.
- I know, too. That's why I said it.

37:55.205 --> 37:56.638
- Oh! We lost them.
- This is going in my report.

37:56.706 --> 37:57.695
No, it's going in my report.

38:20.130 --> 38:24.658
- (LAUGHING) Lando!
- Hey, Han, you crazy old bastard.

38:24.734 --> 38:27.328
Hey, let me introduce everybody.
You remember Chewbacca.

38:27.404 --> 38:32.273
And this is my special friend, Leia.
And that's Sarge over there.

38:32.409 --> 38:34.934
You don't know my name, do you?
You never bothered to learn it.

38:35.011 --> 38:36.342
What are you talking about?

38:36.413 --> 38:39.143
We've been through
all kinds of space adventures together.

38:39.215 --> 38:40.705
Of course I know you, slugger.

38:40.784 --> 38:43.776
- Yeah, sure. Nice to meet you. I'm C-3PO.
- C-3PO, yeah.

38:43.853 --> 38:46.686
I was just gonna introduce you, C-3PO.
Why didn't you let me, C-3PO?

38:46.756 --> 38:48.690
Maybe we should go inside.

38:48.758 --> 38:50.123
Yeah, let's get inside, C-3PO.

38:50.193 --> 38:52.218
You ever been to Cloud City, C-3PO?

39:11.548 --> 39:14.312
J.Crew outlet store.
Oh, my God! Awesome!

39:14.384 --> 39:16.682
Space summer is right around the corner.

39:22.726 --> 39:24.591
Oh, my God. What happened?

39:24.661 --> 39:28.859
I got into a slap fight with a prep droid
over a pair of cargo shorts.

39:28.932 --> 39:30.524
Are you guys all ready for dinner?

39:30.600 --> 39:33.091
I don't know,
the time change is really hitting me.

39:33.169 --> 39:35.433
I might just stay in the room
and watch bad TV.

39:35.505 --> 39:38.497
Geez, it's only like two hours earlier
on Hoth. What's the big deal?

39:38.575 --> 39:40.736
I'm having my period, okay?

39:40.810 --> 39:44.211
Please come in.
I have nothing to say to Lando.

39:47.984 --> 39:50.509
Okay, the door's gonna open
and you guys say, "Freeze,"

39:50.587 --> 39:51.747
and point your guns at them.

39:51.821 --> 39:53.618
Or, you know... Or should it just be me?

39:53.690 --> 39:55.282
Yeah, you know what?
I think that'll be better.

39:55.358 --> 39:57.826
Get out. Go, go, go. It's just me.

39:58.528 --> 40:00.120
I wasn't ready. Hi!

40:00.230 --> 40:01.561
(EXCLAIMS)

40:03.900 --> 40:05.333
(SINGING) Wonder Woman

40:08.071 --> 40:11.063
(JEERING ) Look,
the Giant Chicken's Boba Fett.

40:15.011 --> 40:17.104
DARTH VADER: Very well, Solo,
if you won't talk,

40:17.180 --> 40:19.944
we have very effective means of torture.

40:20.016 --> 40:22.507
Whoa! Well, I don't want to be tortured.

40:22.585 --> 40:25.110
All right, Luke's on Dagobah,
there's a Rebel base on Kashyyyk,

40:25.188 --> 40:27.588
and I'm the one
who clogged the toilet on the 16th floor.

40:27.657 --> 40:29.318
That was disgusting!

40:29.392 --> 40:32.486
You know, because of that, I had to use
the little pig people's bathroom.

40:32.629 --> 40:34.028
All right, start the torture.

40:36.533 --> 40:37.591
(WHERE HAVE ALL THE COWBOYS
GONE PLAYING)

40:37.667 --> 40:41.569
WOMAN: (SINGING)
Where have all the cowboys gone?

40:41.638 --> 40:44.198
(SHOUTING IN DISGUST)
Shut it off. Shut it off!

40:45.642 --> 40:47.166
(HAN SCREAMING)

40:48.945 --> 40:50.276
HAN: Ow!

40:50.346 --> 40:53.281
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

40:53.349 --> 40:54.816
Ow! Ow!

40:55.285 --> 40:56.343
Ow!

40:56.586 --> 40:57.575
Ow!

41:01.825 --> 41:03.417
DARTH VADER: This facility
should be adequate

41:03.493 --> 41:06.223
to freeze Skywalker
for his trip to the Emperor.

41:06.296 --> 41:08.423
We'll test it on Captain Solo.

41:08.498 --> 41:09.829
And as long as we're freezing things,

41:09.899 --> 41:12.800
why don't you toss this ice cube tray
full of orange juice in there?

41:12.869 --> 41:14.564
And be careful with the toothpicks.

41:14.671 --> 41:16.605
Lando, Lando. Lando!

41:17.240 --> 41:19.105
Be careful with the toothpicks.

41:25.548 --> 41:28.449
Chewie, you have to take care
of the princess while I'm gone.

41:28.551 --> 41:29.848
Take care of her?

41:29.919 --> 41:32.251
- You mean like...
- No. What?

41:32.322 --> 41:33.846
No. Just make sure she stays safe.

41:33.923 --> 41:36.084
Okay. That'll be fun for me.

41:44.634 --> 41:45.896
I love you.

41:46.603 --> 41:47.763
Fuck off.

42:39.589 --> 42:42.023
(AMERICAN IDOL THEME PLAYING)

42:42.091 --> 42:43.820
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

42:43.893 --> 42:48.057
Ladies and gentlemen,
this is your lightsaber battle.

42:51.334 --> 42:53.928
The Force is with you, young Skywalker.

42:54.003 --> 42:56.198
But you are not a Jedi yet.

42:56.706 --> 42:58.367
You're getting there.
You're getting there, though.

42:58.441 --> 43:01.342
I can defeat you, Vader. You'll see.

43:05.014 --> 43:08.006
Okay, so, no cutting off body parts.
Let's make that a rule.

43:08.084 --> 43:10.314
No below the belt,
if you know what I'm saying.

43:10.420 --> 43:12.547
And you know what?
How about no name calling?

43:12.622 --> 43:16.080
You know, let's not have
one of those kinds of lightsaber battles.

43:28.171 --> 43:30.139
Car. Car coming!

43:31.908 --> 43:33.239
We're clear.

43:43.853 --> 43:45.115
(BEEPING)

43:48.124 --> 43:52.618
Nice work, fellas! And, David,
you sold the most magazine subscriptions,

43:52.695 --> 43:56.028
so you get to invite
four of your friends to a pizza party.

43:56.099 --> 43:57.259
Hurray!

43:59.402 --> 44:03.099
- Put Captain Solo in the cargo hold.
- Duh!

44:18.588 --> 44:22.456
Oh, no. We've lost Han.
They're taking him to Jabba's palace.

44:22.525 --> 44:24.618
Well, even though
we know exactly where he's going,

44:24.694 --> 44:26.423
we should rescue him in three years.

44:52.855 --> 44:55.551
(GASPING) Oh, God. Oh, my God.

44:55.625 --> 44:59.618
I would give my right hand
for this day to just end.

45:02.799 --> 45:06.633
Oh, no. Damn it.
They changed the security code.

45:06.703 --> 45:09.729
Let me see
if I can do something about that.

45:10.640 --> 45:13.837
Hey, baby.
You're gonna let us through, ain't you?

45:14.310 --> 45:17.279
Yeah, that's right.
You know that feels good.

45:17.346 --> 45:21.373
FEMALE VOICE: Oh, God!
Nobody's touched me like that for so long.

45:21.451 --> 45:22.941
(MOANING EXCITEDLY)

45:23.019 --> 45:26.352
- Oh, no! I think I hear my husband.
- Honey, I'm home.

45:26.422 --> 45:29.220
(SHOUTING) What the hell is this?
Who's he?

45:29.292 --> 45:32.420
Thank God you're home, honey.
He tried to rape me.

45:32.495 --> 45:33.587
Oh, that's bullshit.

45:33.663 --> 45:34.994
You get out of our home!

45:40.636 --> 45:43.366
Oh, man.
How am I supposed to run with this?

45:59.789 --> 46:01.620
Have we ever hit anybody with these guns?

46:01.791 --> 46:03.088
I hit a bird once.

46:03.259 --> 46:04.988
(LIGHTSABERS HUMMING)

46:08.698 --> 46:10.029
(GRUNTING)

46:12.335 --> 46:15.634
Come on, Luke,
join the dark side. It's really cool.

46:15.705 --> 46:17.036
Well, who's in it?

46:17.874 --> 46:21.867
Me, the Emperor, this guy Scott.
You'll meet him, he's awesome.

46:21.944 --> 46:23.502
And James Caan.

46:23.579 --> 46:25.672
I'll be your friend
if you let me kick your ass.

46:25.748 --> 46:28.945
I'll never join the dark side. Never!

46:30.686 --> 46:32.017
(GRUNTING)

46:35.258 --> 46:36.623
(GROANING)

46:38.728 --> 46:40.195
MAN: Hey, a hand.

46:41.931 --> 46:45.697
There is no escape.
Don't make me destroy you.

46:45.768 --> 46:49.169
- Join me, Luke.
- I'll never join you.

46:49.539 --> 46:52.736
Obi-Wan never told you
what happened to your father.

46:52.809 --> 46:54.606
He told me you killed him.

46:54.677 --> 46:56.474
No, I... Hang on.

46:56.546 --> 46:57.740
Spoiler alert.

46:57.814 --> 47:01.306
Okay. No, I am your father.

47:01.384 --> 47:03.545
Well, that's fine,
but I don't see how that affects...

47:03.619 --> 47:05.553
What?

47:05.621 --> 47:09.557
Join me and we can rule the galaxy
as father and son!

47:09.625 --> 47:13.527
You know? I mean, it doesn't have to be
as father and son, it can just be as,

47:13.596 --> 47:16.565
you know, as two really close guys
who just happen to be men, you know?

47:16.632 --> 47:19.863
Just two good-looking guys
sharing a cramped office,

47:19.936 --> 47:22.200
running the galaxy together, you know?

47:22.271 --> 47:24.933
Just getting the job done, you know?
Maybe we...

47:25.007 --> 47:27.202
Maybe we'd do it occasionally,
but it's not weird, you know,

47:27.276 --> 47:30.768
'cause we're just two guys
with raging goals, you know?

47:30.947 --> 47:32.414
I mean, it's not even about
the doing it part,

47:32.481 --> 47:34.711
but that's a part of it,
but it's not the whole thing.

47:49.999 --> 47:51.364
(SCREAMING)

47:59.175 --> 48:02.042
Hey, did you see a hand come down here?

48:02.111 --> 48:03.135
No.

48:05.214 --> 48:06.340
(LUKE SCREAMING)

48:11.754 --> 48:13.085
(GRUNTING)

48:15.524 --> 48:18.254
Ben. Ben.

48:18.794 --> 48:21.490
Leia. Leia.

48:22.365 --> 48:23.832
Tom Selleck.

48:32.708 --> 48:33.697
Leia.

48:38.214 --> 48:41.706
Luke. Turn the ship around.
I know where Luke is.

48:41.784 --> 48:43.581
What, are you out of your mind?
What about those fighters?

48:43.653 --> 48:45.177
I said turn us around!

48:45.254 --> 48:48.815
WOMAN: (SINGING) Turn the ship around

48:48.891 --> 48:52.418
Leia knows where Luke is

48:52.495 --> 48:56.261
Turn it upside down

48:56.332 --> 49:00.462
Take it back to Bespin

49:01.237 --> 49:02.329
Is that him?

49:02.405 --> 49:03.838
LEIA: I don't know.

49:04.206 --> 49:07.972
Luke, if that's you, wave your right hand!

49:08.511 --> 49:10.172
No, your right hand.

49:10.246 --> 49:12.009
LUKE: It's me, you fuckers!

49:46.782 --> 49:48.716
- Luke.
- Yeah.

49:49.251 --> 49:50.377
- Luke?
- Yeah?

49:50.619 --> 49:52.450
- Wait. Luke Skywalker?
- Yeah.

49:52.788 --> 49:55.621
Oh, my God! This is so stupid,
I was trying to call Luke Adams.

49:55.691 --> 49:58.717
His number is right next to yours
in my helmet.

49:59.562 --> 50:02.053
So, how's everything been going
since our fight?

50:03.099 --> 50:04.123
It's good.

50:04.200 --> 50:06.634
And, you know,
the offer's still open for the whole

50:06.702 --> 50:08.670
"two dudes running the galaxy" plan.

50:08.738 --> 50:10.467
Yeah, listen, I gotta go.

50:10.539 --> 50:12.166
Sure, sure, you're busy. It's okay.

50:12.375 --> 50:16.004
All right. Well, I'll talk to you
later, Luke Skywalker, right?

50:16.078 --> 50:17.511
- Yeah.
- Okay.

50:27.423 --> 50:30.017
Prepare to lock the tractor beam
onto the Millennium Falcon.

50:30.493 --> 50:32.518
All right, Chewie, punch it!

50:38.401 --> 50:40.631
Oh, man. All right,
someone's getting choked over this.

50:40.703 --> 50:42.193
Who was in charge of the tractor beam?

50:42.271 --> 50:43.329
That was me.

50:43.406 --> 50:44.532
Oh, yeah? Well...

50:44.907 --> 50:47.467
You have failed me for the last time.

50:49.412 --> 50:52.404
- I can still breathe just fine.
- I know.

50:52.481 --> 50:55.109
- You're choking my...
- Yup. 'Cause I'm upset with you.

50:56.085 --> 50:57.609
For the tractor beam thing.

51:09.932 --> 51:12.958
Don't worry, we'll find Jabba the Hutt
and that bounty hunter,

51:13.035 --> 51:14.969
and we'll get Han back.

51:15.337 --> 51:17.737
Why are you wearing Han's clothes?

51:17.807 --> 51:19.331
Seriously, watch the actual movie.

51:19.408 --> 51:22.605
Lando is wearing Han's clothes
in this scene. It's really weird.

51:23.712 --> 51:27.341
Take care, you two.
May the Force be with you.

51:27.416 --> 51:30.283
CHEWIE: There he goes with that crap
again. Keep it in church, man.

51:32.288 --> 51:34.381
All right. Is this thing good to go?

51:34.457 --> 51:36.288
Yeah, but practice on a hot dog first.

51:36.358 --> 51:37.723
Otherwise you might rip your dick off.

51:41.464 --> 51:45.298
ARTOO: Someday, I'm gonna buy my moms
a place with a view like this.

51:47.770 --> 51:49.897
(INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

52:16.132 --> 52:17.360
(MUSIC STOPS)

52:17.433 --> 52:19.833
Wait a minute. This is how it ends?

52:19.902 --> 52:22.370
There's so many questions
left unanswered.

52:22.505 --> 52:23.836
Are you Luke Skywalker?

52:24.273 --> 52:26.901
- Yeah.
- I've got something for you.

52:26.976 --> 52:28.204
A letter.

52:30.045 --> 52:32.707
"Dear Luke, if my calculations are correct,

52:32.781 --> 52:36.342
"you should receive this letter at the exact
moment the DeLorean vanished.

52:36.418 --> 52:40.855
"I have been living happily
for the past six months in the year 1885.

52:40.923 --> 52:41.981
"The lightning bolt that..."

52:42.057 --> 52:45.151
(GASPS) 1885! The doc's alive!

52:45.227 --> 52:48.025
I mean, he's in the Old West,
but he's alive!

52:59.375 --> 53:01.104
The end.

53:01.577 --> 53:03.101
(ALL CHEERING)

53:03.445 --> 53:05.845
Well, let's see Robot Chicken top this one.

53:05.915 --> 53:09.043
Actually, I think they did a pretty good job
of that already, Dad.

53:09.118 --> 53:12.087
Well, I'll have to take your word for it.
I don't watch Comedy Central.

53:12.154 --> 53:15.715
It's on Cartoon Network's Adult Swim, Dad.
I'm pretty sure you know that.

53:15.791 --> 53:18.055
I don't know that.
I haven't seen that show in a while

53:18.127 --> 53:19.719
and I don't know that anyone else has.

53:19.795 --> 53:22.855
I think plenty of people have.
Their fans are pretty loyal to them.

53:22.932 --> 53:24.729
Oh, yeah? All 42 of them?

53:24.800 --> 53:27.200
(SIGHS) I'm not gonna let you get to me
this time, Dad.

53:27.269 --> 53:28.668
I'm not gonna let you get to me.

53:28.737 --> 53:30.705
Well, maybe I got time
for another story then.

53:30.773 --> 53:32.035
It's called Without A Paddle.

53:32.107 --> 53:33.870
Fuck you, Dad!

54:39.775 --> 54:40.764
OCR, Spell Checked by Ikatiz

54:40.765 --> 55:41.765
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru